ders including dementia or seizures \nActive uncontrolled infection \nOther serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study \nConcomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, or concomitant chemotherapy, hormonal therapy, or immunotherapy \nconcomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. \ni. Warfarin, phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nOther tumor type than adenocarcinoma \nCentral nervous system (CNS) metastases [OR] or prior radiation for CNS metastases \nGastric outlet obstruction [OR] or intestinal obstruction \nEvidence of gastrointestinal bleeding \nThe patient has bony lesions as the sole evaluable disease. \nPast [OR] or concurrent history of neoplasm other than stomach cancer, except for curatively treated [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer [OR] or in situ carcinoma of the cervix uteri \nPregnant [OR] or lactating women, women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] not employing adequate contraception \nOther serious illness [OR] or medical conditions \nUnstable cardiac disease [AND] despite treatment, myocardial infarction within 6 months prior to study entry \nHistory of significant neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disorders including dementia [OR] or seizures \nActive uncontrolled infection \nOther serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study \nConcomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, [OR] or concomitant chemotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy, [OR] or immunotherapy \nconcomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. \ni. Warfarin, [OR] phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: [NOT] inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1<|eot_id|>']
Response: Other tumor type than adenocarcinoma 
Central nervous system (CNS) metastases [OR] or prior radiation for CNS metastases 
Gastric outlet obstruction [OR] or intestinal obstruction 
Evidence of gastrointestinal bleeding 
The patient has bony lesions as the sole evaluable disease. 
Past [OR] or concurrent history of neoplasm other than stomach cancer, except for curatively treated [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer [OR] or in situ carcinoma of the cervix uteri 
Pregnant [OR] or lactating women, women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] not employing adequate contraception 
Other serious illness [OR] or medical conditions 
Unstable cardiac disease [AND] despite treatment, myocardial infarction within 6 months prior to study entry 
History of significant neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disorders including dementia [OR] or seizures 
Active uncontrolled infection 
Other serious underlying medical conditions which could impair the ability of the patient to participate in the study 
Concomitant administration of any other experimental drug under investigation, [OR] or concomitant chemotherapy, [OR] hormonal therapy, [OR] or immunotherapy 
concomitant drug medication; The following drugs cause drug interaction with S-1. 
i. Warfarin, [OR] phenprocoumon: increase bleeding tendency ii. Increase blood concentration of phenytoin iii. sorivudine: [NOT] inhibit DPD -> increase toxicity according to fluoropyrimidine iv. allopurinol : decrease activity of S-1
