Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHistologically or cytologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the breast with locally advanced or metastatic disease, and a candidate for chemotherapy. \nHuman epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-positive. \nNo prior chemotherapy for their metastatic breast cancer (MBC). \nMeasurable disease. \nAge ≥ 18 years. \nFor women of childbearing potential and men with partners of childbearing potential, agreement to use a highly effective, non-hormonal form of contraception or 2 effective forms of non-hormonal contraception by the patient and/or partner. Contraception use must continue for the duration of study treatment and for at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment. Male patients whose partners are pregnant should use condoms for the duration of the study. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHistologically [OR] or cytologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the breast [AND] with locally advanced [OR] or metastatic disease, [AND] and a candidate for chemotherapy.\nHuman epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-positive.\n [NOT] No prior chemotherapy [AND] for their metastatic breast cancer (MBC).\nMeasurable disease.\nAge ≥ 18 years.\nFor women [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] and men [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement to use a highly effective, [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception [OR] or 2 effective forms of [NOT] non-hormonal contraception by the patient and/or partner. Contraception use must continue for the duration of study treatment [AND] and for at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment. Male patients [AND] whose partners are pregnant should use condoms for the duration of the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Histologically [OR] or cytologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the breast [AND] with locally advanced [OR] or metastatic disease, [AND] and a candidate for chemotherapy.
Human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-positive.
 [NOT] No prior chemotherapy [AND] for their metastatic breast cancer (MBC).
Measurable disease.
Age ≥ 18 years.
For women [AND] of childbearing potential [AND] and men [AND] with partners of childbearing potential, agreement to use a highly effective, [NOT] non-hormonal form of contraception [OR] or 2 effective forms of [NOT] non-hormonal contraception by the patient and/or partner. Contraception use must continue for the duration of study treatment [AND] and for at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment. Male patients [AND] whose partners are pregnant should use condoms for the duration of the study.
