00 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent \n\n\n### Response:\nHLA-A2 melanoma patients with : \neither loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis \ntransit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable \nmeasurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis \nPatients\' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. \n[NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. \n [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. \nLife expectancy should be greater than 6 months. \nGeneral state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. \nPatient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. \nBiological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. \nSigned informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: HLA-A2 melanoma patients with : 
either loco-regional [OR] or lymph node metastasis 
transit nodules [NOT] not surgically resectable 
measurable cutaneous [OR] or visceral metastasis 
Patients' tumor express Melan-A/ [OR] MART-1 antigen. 
[NOT] No chemotherapy treatment (except for Deticene used before the first T cell clones infusion) [OR] or radiotherapy [OR] or immunotherapy in the last 4 weeks before infusion. 
 [NOT] No other melanoma treatment during the protocol. 
Life expectancy should be greater than 6 months. 
General state with Karnowsky greater than 80, ECOG = 0, 1 or 2. 
Patient should be negative for HIV [OR] and B [OR] and C hepatitis. 
Biological parameters at the beginning of the study: leucocytes ³ 2000 elements per mm3, hemoglobin ³ 10.5g/dl, platelets ³ 100 000 per mm3, phosphatases alcalines transaminases £ 1 time 1/2 compared to the normal. 
Signed informed consent
