Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nCytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)\nNo relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL\nPatients must meet one of the following risk criteria:\nStandard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8\nAged 1 to < 6 years\nInitial WBC < 20,000/µL\nM1 (5%) or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;\nM1 marrow on day 33.\nAged < 1 or = 6 years and/or WBC = 20,000/µL\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\nM1 or M2 marrow on day 15\nM3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 OR meets SR criteria but M3 marrow on day 15 and *M1 marrow on day 33.\nMeets IR criteria and M3 marrow on day 15 (not SR and M3 on day 15)\nBlasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\nM2 or M3 marrow on day 33\nTranslocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].\n\n\n### Response:\nCytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)\n [NOT] No relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL\nPatients must meet one of the following risk criteria:\nStandard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8\nAged 1 to < 6 years\nInitial WBC < 20,000/µL\nM1 (5%) [OR] or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;\n M1 marrow on day 33.\nAged < 1 [OR] or = 6 years [OR] and/or WBC = 20,000/µL\nBlasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\n M1 [OR] or M2 marrow on day 15\n M3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 [OR] OR meets SR criteria [AND] but M3 marrow on day 15 [AND] and *M1 marrow on day 33.\nMeets IR criteria [AND] and M3 marrow on day 15 ([NOT] not SR [AND] and M3 on day 15)\nBlasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8\n M2 [OR] or M3 marrow on day 33\nTranslocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) [OR] or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].<|eot_id|>']
Response: Cytologically proven acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL)
 [NOT] No relapse of a previously unrecognized ALL
Patients must meet one of the following risk criteria:
Standard-risk (SR) group meeting all of the following criteria:
Blasts < 1,000/µL in peripheral blood (PB) on day 8
Aged 1 to < 6 years
Initial WBC < 20,000/µL
M1 (5%) [OR] or M2 (= 5% to < 25%) blasts in bone marrow on day 15;
 M1 marrow on day 33.
Aged < 1 [OR] or = 6 years [OR] and/or WBC = 20,000/µL
Blasts < 1,000/µL in PB on day 8
 M1 [OR] or M2 marrow on day 15
 M3 (= 25%) marrow on day 15 [OR] OR meets SR criteria [AND] but M3 marrow on day 15 [AND] and *M1 marrow on day 33.
Meets IR criteria [AND] and M3 marrow on day 15 ([NOT] not SR [AND] and M3 on day 15)
Blasts = 1,000/µL in PB on day 8
 M2 [OR] or M3 marrow on day 33
Translocation t(9;22) [BCR/ABL+] (Philadelphia chromosome-positive) [OR] or t(4;11) [MLL/AF4+].
