Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients with angina or silent ischemia and documented ischemia\nPatients who are eligible for intracoronary stenting\nAge > 18 years\nDe novo lesion CTO\nReference vessel size 2.5 mm by visual estimation\nAt least one CTO lesions located in proximal or mid epicardial coronary artery. (If the patient has two CTO lesions, one CTO lesion should be located in proximal or mid epicardial coronary artery)\nAngiographically defined total occlusion over 3 months\nIf no definite symptom with total occlusion, two experienced operators decide CTO in consideration of angiographical morphology (degree of calcification, bridging collaterals, non-tapered stump, angiographic filling from collaterals)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with angina [OR] or silent ischemia [AND] and documented ischemia\nPatients who are eligible for intracoronary stenting\nAge > 18 years\nDe novo lesion CTO\nReference vessel size 2.5 mm by visual estimation\nAt least one CTO lesions located in proximal [OR] or mid epicardial coronary artery. (If the patient has two CTO lesions, one CTO lesion should be located in proximal [OR] or mid epicardial coronary artery)\nAngiographically defined total occlusion over 3 months\nIf [NOT] no definite symptom with total occlusion, two experienced operators decide CTO in consideration of angiographical morphology (degree of calcification, [OR] bridging collaterals, [NOT] non-tapered stump, angiographic filling from collaterals)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with angina [OR] or silent ischemia [AND] and documented ischemia
Patients who are eligible for intracoronary stenting
Age > 18 years
De novo lesion CTO
Reference vessel size 2.5 mm by visual estimation
At least one CTO lesions located in proximal [OR] or mid epicardial coronary artery. (If the patient has two CTO lesions, one CTO lesion should be located in proximal [OR] or mid epicardial coronary artery)
Angiographically defined total occlusion over 3 months
If [NOT] no definite symptom with total occlusion, two experienced operators decide CTO in consideration of angiographical morphology (degree of calcification, [OR] bridging collaterals, [NOT] non-tapered stump, angiographic filling from collaterals)
