of fetal cytomegalovirus infection\n  -  birth asphyxia\n  -  a history of major head injury\n  -  a chronic use of [NOT] non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, (NSAID)\n  -  known brain damage\n  -  Epilepsy\n  -  Abnormal Electro-cardiogram (ECG)\n  -  Epileptiform EEG\nUse of psychostimulants, [OR] anti-depressants, [OR] neuroleptics [OR] or anti-convulsive agents within the past month.\nLack of cooperation in the screening phase<|eot_id|>']
