Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSurgery and/or previous ocular pathology (presence of scar/change in the cornea, glaucoma, retinopathies, etc.). \nPatient has diabetes or is immunodepressed. \nAny systemic infection during the study. \nSigns and/or symptoms of ocular inflammation/infection (bacterial, viral, fungal, caused by Chlamydia, by Mycobacterium, Acanthamoeba or of allergic etiology). \nHave used any systemic or topical antibiotics for ocular infection in the previous 14 days. \nPatient has known hypersensitivity to any of the components of the formulations used in the study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nSurgery [OR] and/or previous ocular pathology (presence of scar/ [OR] change in the cornea, [OR] glaucoma, [OR] retinopathies, etc.). \nPatient has diabetes [OR] or is immunodepressed. \nAny systemic infection during the study. \nSigns [OR] and/or symptoms of ocular inflammation/ [OR] infection (bacterial, [OR] viral, [OR] fungal, caused by Chlamydia, [OR] by Mycobacterium, [OR] Acanthamoeba [OR] or of allergic etiology). \nHave used any systemic [OR] or topical antibiotics for ocular infection in the previous 14 days. \nPatient has known hypersensitivity to any of the components of the formulations used in the study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Surgery [OR] and/or previous ocular pathology (presence of scar/ [OR] change in the cornea, [OR] glaucoma, [OR] retinopathies, etc.). 
Patient has diabetes [OR] or is immunodepressed. 
Any systemic infection during the study. 
Signs [OR] and/or symptoms of ocular inflammation/ [OR] infection (bacterial, [OR] viral, [OR] fungal, caused by Chlamydia, [OR] by Mycobacterium, [OR] Acanthamoeba [OR] or of allergic etiology). 
Have used any systemic [OR] or topical antibiotics for ocular infection in the previous 14 days. 
Patient has known hypersensitivity to any of the components of the formulations used in the study.
