deemed necessary. \nEstimated GFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 using the Cockcroft-Gault formula measurement of the individual parameters following at least 5 minutes of rest at Screening.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Subjects with a supine BP >140 mm Hg systolic [OR] or >90 mm Hg diastolic [OR] or <100 mm Hg systolic [OR] or <60 mm Hg diastolic based on the average of the triplicate 
Serum potassium >=5.1 mmol/L [OR] or <3.5 mmol/L at screening, confirmed by a single repeat if deemed necessary. 
Estimated GFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 using the Cockcroft-Gault formula measurement of the individual parameters following at least 5 minutes of rest at Screening.
