File: NCT01518946_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT01518946_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Male and female subjects must be 18 years of age or older and ambulatory. \n2. Females of child-bearing potential (FOCP) must have a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (HCG) pregnancy test. \n3. A documented history of severe Symptomatic Orthostatic Hypotension (SOH) that, in the judgment of the treating physician, has required treatment with midodrine HCl, and has been at a stable dose for at least 3 months. \n4. The subject has manifested at least 1 of the following symptoms while standing or had a medical history of 1 of the following when not treated for orthostatic hypotension (OH): dizziness, lightheadedness, feeling faint, or feeling like they might black out. \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Male [OR] and female subjects must be 18 years of age or older [AND] and ambulatory. \n 2. Females [AND] of child-bearing potential (FOCP) must have a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (HCG) pregnancy test. \n 3. A documented history of severe Symptomatic Orthostatic Hypotension (SOH) that, in the judgment of the treating physician, has required treatment with midodrine HCl, [AND] and has been at a stable dose for at least 3 months. \n 4. The subject has manifested at least 1 of the following symptoms while standing [OR] or had a medical history of 1 of the following when [NOT] not treated for orthostatic hypotension (OH): dizziness, [OR] lightheadedness, [OR] feeling faint, [OR] or feeling like they might black out.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Male [OR] and female subjects must be 18 years of age or older [AND] and ambulatory. 
 2. Females [AND] of child-bearing potential (FOCP) must have a negative serum beta human chorionic gonadotropin (HCG) pregnancy test. 
 3. A documented history of severe Symptomatic Orthostatic Hypotension (SOH) that, in the judgment of the treating physician, has required treatment with midodrine HCl, [AND] and has been at a stable dose for at least 3 months. 
 4. The subject has manifested at least 1 of the following symptoms while standing [OR] or had a medical history of 1 of the following when [NOT] not treated for orthostatic hypotension (OH): dizziness, [OR] lightheadedness, [OR] feeling faint, [OR] or feeling like they might black out.
