File: NCT01701219_exc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT01701219_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. \n2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. \n3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. \n4. Known left-sided endocarditis or prosthetic heart valve. \n5. Osteomyelitis or prosthetic joint infection except new onset nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. \n6. History of any hypersensitivity or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. \n7. Evidence of significant hepatic, hematologic, or immunologic impairment. \n8. Pregnant or nursing females.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. \n2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. \n3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. \n4. Known left-sided endocarditis [OR] or prosthetic heart valve. \n5. Osteomyelitis [OR] or prosthetic joint infection except new onset [NOT] nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. \n6. History of any hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. \n7. Evidence of significant hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] or immunologic impairment. \n8. Pregnant [OR] or nursing females.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
1. For subjects in Cohort A: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against S. aureus within 72 hours of positive blood culture results. 
2. For subjects in Cohort B: previous therapy for more than 48 hours with any parenteral antibiotic [AND] with activity against MRSA, except vancomycin [OR] and/or daptomycin, within 72 hours of positive blood culture results confirming persistence. 
3. Previous episode of S. aureus bacteremia within 3 months. 
4. Known left-sided endocarditis [OR] or prosthetic heart valve. 
5. Osteomyelitis [OR] or prosthetic joint infection except new onset [NOT] nonhardware-associated vertebral osteomyelitis. 
6. History of any hypersensitivity [OR] or allergic reaction to any β-lactam antibacterial agent. 
7. Evidence of significant hepatic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] or immunologic impairment. 
8. Pregnant [OR] or nursing females.
