Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHealthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by absence of evidence of any active or chronic disease following a detailed medical and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, blood chemistry, serology and urinalysis \nBody mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive \nMale subjects (whether surgically sterilized or not) with female partners of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study and for 77 days after the last dose \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHealthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis \nBody mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive \nMale subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Healthy male volunteers, 18 to 45 years of age, inclusive. Healthy status is defined by [NOT] absence of evidence of any active [OR] or chronic disease following a detailed medical [OR] and surgical history, a complete physical examination including vital signs, 12-lead ECG, hematology, [OR] blood chemistry, [OR] serology [OR] and urinalysis 
Body mass index (BMI) 18 to 30 kg/m2 inclusive 
Male subjects (whether surgically sterilized [OR] or [NOT] not) [AND] with female partners [AND] of child-bearing potential must use two forms of contraception, one of which must be a barrier method, for the duration of the study [AND] and for 77 days after the last dose
