Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT01757717_exc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients who may receive therapeutically effective doses via an external beam approach to the lesion of interest as specified by MSKCC Radiation Oncology Department dose constraint criteria. \nPatients with kyphoplasty cement or hardware that would preclude effective catheter placement. \nPatients with paraspinal extension of disease with visceral involvement. \nAbnormal complete blood count. Any of the following: \nPlatelet count < 75,000/ml \nHb level < 9gm/dl \nWBC < 3.5/ml \nAbnormal coagulation profile: INR > 2.5 and/or PTT > 80 \nPatients who are on anticoagulation medication that may not be safely held for the procedure (≥ 5 days for antiplatelet agents and warfarin; ≥ 24 hours for low-molecular weight heparin formulations) will be excluded. \nContraindications to general anesthesia       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients who may receive therapeutically effective doses via an external beam approach to the lesion of interest as specified by MSKCC Radiation Oncology Department dose constraint criteria. \nExclusion Criteria:\nPatients with kyphoplasty cement [OR] or hardware that would [NOT] preclude effective catheter placement. \nPatients with paraspinal extension of disease [AND] with visceral involvement. \nAbnormal complete blood count. Any of the following: \nPlatelet count < 75,000/ml \nHb level < 9gm/dl \nWBC < 3.5/ml \nAbnormal coagulation profile: INR > 2.5 [OR] and/or PTT > 80 \nPatients who are on anticoagulation medication that may [NOT] not be safely held for the procedure (≥ 5 days for antiplatelet agents [OR] and warfarin; ≥ 24 hours for low-molecular weight heparin formulations) will be [NOT] excluded. \nContraindications to general anesthesia<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients who may receive therapeutically effective doses via an external beam approach to the lesion of interest as specified by MSKCC Radiation Oncology Department dose constraint criteria. 
Exclusion Criteria:
Patients with kyphoplasty cement [OR] or hardware that would [NOT] preclude effective catheter placement. 
Patients with paraspinal extension of disease [AND] with visceral involvement. 
Abnormal complete blood count. Any of the following: 
Platelet count < 75,000/ml 
Hb level < 9gm/dl 
WBC < 3.5/ml 
Abnormal coagulation profile: INR > 2.5 [OR] and/or PTT > 80 
Patients who are on anticoagulation medication that may [NOT] not be safely held for the procedure (≥ 5 days for antiplatelet agents [OR] and warfarin; ≥ 24 hours for low-molecular weight heparin formulations) will be [NOT] excluded. 
Contraindications to general anesthesia
