Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAge 18 or older\nWilling and able to comply with the study procedures and provide written informed consent to participate in the study\nDiagnosis of probable pancreatic cancer, distal common bile duct (CBD) cholangiocarcinoma and other periampullary cancers (histology not required)\nBiliary obstructive symptoms or signs\nBilirubin level at/above 100 umol per liter (5.8 mg/dL)\nDistal biliary obstruction consistent with pancreatic cancer, distal CBD cholangiocarcinoma or other periampullary malignancy\nLocation of distal biliary obstruction is such that it would allow the proximal end of a stent to be positioned at least 2cm from the hilum\nPatients deemed as resectable by pancreatic protocol CT or MRI\nSurgical candidate per pancreatobiliary surgeon after multi-disciplinary discussion\nSurgery intent within 4 weeks\nEndoscopic and surgical treatment to be provided by same team\n\n\n### Response:\nAge 18 or older\nWilling and able to comply with the study procedures and provide written informed consent to participate in the study\nDiagnosis of probable pancreatic cancer, [OR] distal common bile duct (CBD) cholangiocarcinoma [OR] and other periampullary cancers (histology [NOT] not required)\nBiliary obstructive symptoms [OR] or signs\nBilirubin level at/above 100 umol per liter (5.8 mg/dL)\nDistal biliary obstruction consistent with pancreatic cancer, [OR] distal CBD cholangiocarcinoma [OR] or other periampullary malignancy\nLocation of distal biliary obstruction is such that it would allow the proximal end of a stent to be positioned at least 2cm from the hilum\nPatients deemed as resectable by pancreatic protocol CT [OR] or MRI\nSurgical candidate per pancreatobiliary surgeon after multi-disciplinary discussion\nSurgery intent within 4 weeks\nEndoscopic [AND] and surgical treatment to be provided by same team<|eot_id|>']
Response: Age 18 or older
Willing and able to comply with the study procedures and provide written informed consent to participate in the study
Diagnosis of probable pancreatic cancer, [OR] distal common bile duct (CBD) cholangiocarcinoma [OR] and other periampullary cancers (histology [NOT] not required)
Biliary obstructive symptoms [OR] or signs
Bilirubin level at/above 100 umol per liter (5.8 mg/dL)
Distal biliary obstruction consistent with pancreatic cancer, [OR] distal CBD cholangiocarcinoma [OR] or other periampullary malignancy
Location of distal biliary obstruction is such that it would allow the proximal end of a stent to be positioned at least 2cm from the hilum
Patients deemed as resectable by pancreatic protocol CT [OR] or MRI
Surgical candidate per pancreatobiliary surgeon after multi-disciplinary discussion
Surgery intent within 4 weeks
Endoscopic [AND] and surgical treatment to be provided by same team
