Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nHad dose increase of anti-TNF agent or DMARD in the last 6 months\nHad change of anti-TNF agent or DMARD in the last 6 months\nTreated currently with golimumab or certolizumab\nTreated with greater than 10 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 6 months\nTreated with greater than 5 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 3 months\nTreated with intramuscular or intravenous corticosteroids in the last 6 months for RA activity\nTreated with anakinra, abatacept, or tocilizumab in the last 6 months\nTreated with rituximab in the last 12 months\nTreated with an investigational RA drug in the last 6 months\nPregnant (or anticipate pregnancy during the study period) or lactating women\nAbsence of documentation in the medical record of clinical remission for the last 6 months\nUnwilling to discontinue anti-TNF agent\nAbsence of documentation of negative tuberculin skin test, negative QuantiFERON-TB Gold test, or treatment for latent tuberculosis prior to starting treatment with the anti-TNF agent\nTreatment of solid malignancy or non-melanoma skin cancer within the past 5 years, or any history of melanoma or hematologic or lymphoproliferative malignancy\nAbsence of documentation of age-appropriate cancer screening at the time of randomization\nAbsence of documentation of negative hepatitis B serologies, absence of completion of treatment for chronic hepatitis B, or absence of suppressive antiviral treatment\nUnable to provide informed consent\nAnticipate not being available or able to comply with the schedule of study visits\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nHad dose increase of anti-TNF agent [OR] or DMARD in the last 6 months\nHad change of anti-TNF agent [OR] or DMARD in the last 6 months\nTreated currently with golimumab [OR] or certolizumab\nTreated with greater than 10 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 6 months\nTreated with greater than 5 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 3 months\nTreated with intramuscular [OR] or intravenous corticosteroids in the last 6 months for RA activity\nTreated with anakinra, [OR] abatacept, [OR] or tocilizumab in the last 6 months\nTreated with rituximab in the last 12 months\nTreated with an investigational RA drug in the last 6 months\nPregnant (or anticipate pregnancy during the study period) [OR] or lactating women\n [NOT] Absence of documentation in the medical record of clinical remission for the last 6 months\nUnwilling to [NOT] discontinue anti-TNF agent\n [NOT] Absence of documentation of negative tuberculin skin test, negative QuantiFERON-TB Gold test, [OR] or treatment for latent tuberculosis prior to starting treatment with the anti-TNF agent\nTreatment of solid malignancy [OR] or [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer within the past 5 years, [OR] or any history of melanoma [OR] or hematologic [OR] or lymphoproliferative malignancy\n [NOT] Absence of documentation of age-appropriate cancer screening at the time of randomization\n [NOT] Absence of documentation of negative hepatitis B serologies, [NOT] absence of completion of treatment for chronic hepatitis B, [OR] or [NOT] absence of suppressive antiviral treatment\nUnable to provide informed consent\nAnticipate [NOT] not being available [OR] or able to comply with the schedule of study visits<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Had dose increase of anti-TNF agent [OR] or DMARD in the last 6 months
Had change of anti-TNF agent [OR] or DMARD in the last 6 months
Treated currently with golimumab [OR] or certolizumab
Treated with greater than 10 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 6 months
Treated with greater than 5 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) daily in the last 3 months
Treated with intramuscular [OR] or intravenous corticosteroids in the last 6 months for RA activity
Treated with anakinra, [OR] abatacept, [OR] or tocilizumab in the last 6 months
Treated with rituximab in the last 12 months
Treated with an investigational RA drug in the last 6 months
Pregnant (or anticipate pregnancy during the study period) [OR] or lactating women
 [NOT] Absence of documentation in the medical record of clinical remission for the last 6 months
Unwilling to [NOT] discontinue anti-TNF agent
 [NOT] Absence of documentation of negative tuberculin skin test, negative QuantiFERON-TB Gold test, [OR] or treatment for latent tuberculosis prior to starting treatment with the anti-TNF agent
Treatment of solid malignancy [OR] or [NOT] non-melanoma skin cancer within the past 5 years, [OR] or any history of melanoma [OR] or hematologic [OR] or lymphoproliferative malignancy
 [NOT] Absence of documentation of age-appropriate cancer screening at the time of randomization
 [NOT] Absence of documentation of negative hepatitis B serologies, [NOT] absence of completion of treatment for chronic hepatitis B, [OR] or [NOT] absence of suppressive antiviral treatment
Unable to provide informed consent
Anticipate [NOT] not being available [OR] or able to comply with the schedule of study visits
