Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatient is currently participating in a Novartis Oncology sponsored study receiving pasireotide (LAR and/or s.c.) and has fulfilled all required assessments in the parent study (unless the study is being terminated) and patients that are benefiting from the study drug have no other alternatives\nPatient is currently benefiting from the treatment with pasireotide, as determined by the investigator\nPatient has demonstrated compliance, as assessed by the investigator, with the parent study requirements\nWillingness and ability to comply with scheduled visits, treatment plans and any other study procedures\nWritten informed consent obtained prior to enrolling in roll-over study and receiving study medication • If consent cannot be expressed in writing, it must be formally documented and witnessed, ideally via an independent trusted witness\n\n\n### Response:\nPatient is currently participating in a Novartis Oncology sponsored study receiving pasireotide (LAR [OR] and/or s.c.) [AND] and has fulfilled all required assessments in the parent study (unless the study is being terminated) [AND] and patients that are benefiting from the study drug have [NOT] no other alternatives\nPatient is currently benefiting from the treatment with pasireotide, as determined by the investigator\nPatient has demonstrated compliance, as assessed by the investigator, with the parent study requirements\nWillingness [AND] and ability to comply with scheduled visits, treatment plans and any other study procedures\nWritten informed consent obtained prior to enrolling in roll-over study and receiving study medication • If consent cannot be expressed in writing, it must be formally documented and witnessed, ideally via an independent trusted witness<|eot_id|>']
Response: Patient is currently participating in a Novartis Oncology sponsored study receiving pasireotide (LAR [OR] and/or s.c.) [AND] and has fulfilled all required assessments in the parent study (unless the study is being terminated) [AND] and patients that are benefiting from the study drug have [NOT] no other alternatives
Patient is currently benefiting from the treatment with pasireotide, as determined by the investigator
Patient has demonstrated compliance, as assessed by the investigator, with the parent study requirements
Willingness [AND] and ability to comply with scheduled visits, treatment plans and any other study procedures
Written informed consent obtained prior to enrolling in roll-over study and receiving study medication • If consent cannot be expressed in writing, it must be formally documented and witnessed, ideally via an independent trusted witness
