Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nany neurological conditions other than PD; \nsignificant musculoskeletal or cardiopulmonary diseases; \nother disorders that may affect balance or locomotion; \ntaken any structured behavioral or exercise programs in the past 3 months \nor they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; \nunstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; \nsurgical interventions for PD; \ncommunication or cognitive deficits with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); \na history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  diagnosed with idiopathic Parkinson\'s disease, (PD);\n  -  the ability to provide informed consent;\n  -  the willingness to participate in the study;\n  -  the ability to fill out questionnaires and test;\n  -  the willingness to be videotaped and audiotaped during the testing procedures;\n  -  the ability to give written informed consent.\nExclusion Criteria:\n - any neurological conditions other than PD; \n - significant musculoskeletal [OR] or cardiopulmonary diseases; \n - other disorders that may affect balance [OR] or locomotion; \n - taken any structured behavioral [OR] or exercise programs in the past 3 months \n - or they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; \n - unstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; \n - surgical interventions for PD;\n - communication [OR] or cognitive deficits [AND] with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); \n - a history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  diagnosed with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, (PD);
  -  the ability to provide informed consent;
  -  the willingness to participate in the study;
  -  the ability to fill out questionnaires and test;
  -  the willingness to be videotaped and audiotaped during the testing procedures;
  -  the ability to give written informed consent.
Exclusion Criteria:
 - any neurological conditions other than PD; 
 - significant musculoskeletal [OR] or cardiopulmonary diseases; 
 - other disorders that may affect balance [OR] or locomotion; 
 - taken any structured behavioral [OR] or exercise programs in the past 3 months 
 - or they are receiving regular physical rehabilitation at present; 
 - unstable condition on anti-parkinsonian medications; 
 - surgical interventions for PD;
 - communication [OR] or cognitive deficits [AND] with mini-mental state examination, (MMSE) <24/30 (Folstein et al., 1975); 
 - a history of more than two falls in the previous 12 months.
