nic or acute hepatitis B infection\nUse of female hormonal products based on estrogen or derivatives\n\n\n### Response:\nPrior receipt of investigational anti-HIV vaccine\nOngoing therapy with any of the following: Systemic corticosteroids. Short course less than or equal to 21 days of corticosteroids is allowed; Systemic chemotherapeutic agents; Nephrotoxic systemic agents, including aminoglycosides, [OR] amphotericin B, [OR] cidofovir, [OR] cisplatin, [OR] foscarnet, [OR] pentamidine; Immunomodulatory treatments including Interleukin-2; Investigational agents\nKnown allergy/ [OR] sensitivity [OR] or any hypersensitivity to components of study drugs (ART) [OR] or their formulations\nActive drug [OR] or alcohol use [OR] or dependence that would interfere with adherence to study requirements\nSerious medical [OR] or psychiatric illness that would interfere with the ability to adhere to study requirements\nChronic [OR] or acute hepatitis B infection\nUse of female hormonal products based on estrogen [OR] or derivatives<|eot_id|>']
