Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients with a confirmed diagnosis of: \n1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy or post-initial chemotherapy or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/leucovorin (5-FU/LV) alone or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease and not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. \n2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection and adjuvant chemotherapy or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy and radiation. Initial chemotherapy or radiation therapy may have been stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. \nPrior surgery, including tumor resection or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. \nNo concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed \nAge >/= 18 years \nPerformance status of 0-1 \nAdequate hepatic, bone marrow, and renal function \nPartial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution\'s normal range and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. \nLife expectancy >/= 4 months for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts \nWomen of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment and must not be lactating. \nSubject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with a confirmed diagnosis of: \n1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy [OR] or post-initial chemotherapy [OR] or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/ [OR] leucovorin (5-FU/ [OR] LV) alone [OR] or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease [AND] and [NOT] not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. \n2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection [OR] and adjuvant chemotherapy [OR] or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy [OR] and radiation. Initial chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy may have been [NOT] stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. \nPrior surgery, including tumor resection [OR] or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. \n[NOT] No concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed \nAge >/= 18 years \nPerformance status of 0-1 \nAdequate hepatic, [OR] bone marrow, [OR] and renal function \nPartial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution\'s normal range [AND] and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. \nLife expectancy >/= 4 months [AND] for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts \nWomen [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment [AND] and must [NOT] not be lactating. \nSubject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with a confirmed diagnosis of: 
1. Stage 4 colon cancer either s/p metastasectomy [OR] or post-initial chemotherapy [OR] or maintenance "standard of care", either involving 5-fluorouracil/ [OR] leucovorin (5-FU/ [OR] LV) alone [OR] or continual bevacizumab alone. Patients in maintenance cohort must have had 2 consecutive CT scans showing stable disease [AND] and [NOT] not be experiencing significant prior treatment-related toxicity above Grade 1. 
2. Pancreas cancer, either s/p resection [OR] and adjuvant chemotherapy [OR] or locally advanced pancreas cancer s/p chemotherapy [OR] and radiation. Initial chemotherapy [OR] or radiation therapy may have been [NOT] stopped between 2 weeks and 2 months prior to study start, and patients must have recovered from prior treatment related toxicity to grade 1 or less. 
Prior surgery, including tumor resection [OR] or metastasectomy must have been performed at least 4 weeks prior to study enrollment. 
[NOT] No concomitant anti-cancer treatment is allowed 
Age >/= 18 years 
Performance status of 0-1 
Adequate hepatic, [OR] bone marrow, [OR] and renal function 
Partial thromboplastin time (PTT) must be </= 1.5 x upper normal limit of institution's normal range [AND] and INR (International Normalized Ratio) < 1.5. 
Life expectancy >/= 4 months [AND] for maintenance cohorts and >/= 6 months for adjuvant cohorts 
Women [AND] of childbearing potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test within 14 days prior to initiation of treatment [AND] and must [NOT] not be lactating. 
Subject is capable of understanding and complying with protocol demands and able to sign and date the informed consent
