onnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n6. Ability to read and write English - \n\n\n### Response:\nCases (with a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) \n6. Ability to read and write English \nControls (without a history of TBI): \n1. Ages 50-95 years \n2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) \n3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville \n4. MMSE score ≥ 20 \n5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research \n6. Ability to read and write English -<|eot_id|>']
Response: Cases (with a history of TBI): 
1. Ages 50-95 years 
2. History of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID, and based on DoD/VA criteria) 
3. Residence in AFRH-Washington D.C. [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
5. Capacity to provide consent to participate in research (assessment made by study physician) 
6. Ability to read and write English 
Controls (without a history of TBI): 
1. Ages 50-95 years 
2. [NOT] No history of traumatic brain injury of sufficient severity to have resulted in medical attention (ascertained via the Ohio State University TBI Identification Questionnaire—OSU TBI-ID) 
3. Residence in AFRH-Washington [OR] or the Veterans Home of California-Yountville 
4. MMSE score ≥ 20 
5. Capacity to provide consent or assent to participate in research 
6. Ability to read and write English -
