Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nintolerance of or allergy to ticagrelor or prasugrel\nhistory of any stroke, transient ischemic attack or intracranial bleeding\nknown intracranial neoplasm, intracranial arteriovenous malformation or intracranial aneurysm\nactive bleeding, clinical findings, that in the judgement of the investigator are associated with an increased risk of bleeding\nfibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 24 h before randomization, non-fibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 48 h before randomization\nknown platelet count < 100.000/µL at the time of screening\nknown anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) at the time of screening\noral anticoagulation that cannot be safely discontinued for the duration of the study\nINR known to be greater than 1.5 at the time of screening\nchronic renal insufficiency requiring dialysis\nmoderate or severe hepatic dysfunction (Child Pugh B or C)\nincreased risk of bradycardia events (Sick Sinus, AV block grade II or III, bradycardia-induced syncope)\nindex event is an acute complication (< 30 days) of PCI\nconcomitant medical illness that in the opinion of the investigator is associated with a life expectancy < 1 year\nconcomitant oral or i.v. therapy with strong CYP3A Inhibitors (e.g. ketoconazole, itraconazole, voriconazole, telithromycin, clarithromycin, nefazodone, ritonavir, saquinavir, nelfinavir, indinavir, atazanavir, grapefruit juice > 1 L/d), CYP3A substrates with narrow therapeutic indices (e.g. cyclosporine, quinidine), or strong CYP3A inducers (e.g. rifampin/rifampicin, phenytoin, carbamazepine, dexamethason, phenobarbital ) that cannot be safely discontinued\n=1 doses of ticagrelor or prasugrel within 5 days before randomisation\nno written informed consent\nparticipation in another investigational drug study\nprevious enrolment in this study\nfor women of childbearing potential no negative pregnancy test and no agree to use reliable method of birth control during the study\nPregnancy, giving birth within the last 90 days, or lactation\ninability to cooperate with protocol requirements\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n  -  men or women aged 18 years or older\n  -  subjects with Acute coronary syndrome (ACS) undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)\n  -  subjects receiving ticagrelor or prasugrel during hospitalization for ACS\n  -  subjects able to give written informed consent\nExclusion Criteria:\n  -  intolerance of [OR] or allergy to ticagrelor [OR] or prasugrel\n  -  history of any stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack [OR] or intracranial bleeding\n  -  known intracranial neoplasm, [OR] intracranial arteriovenous malformation [OR] or intracranial aneurysm\n  -  active bleeding, clinical findings, that in the judgement of the investigator are associated with an increased risk of bleeding\n  -  fibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 24 h before randomization, [NOT] non-fibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 48 h before randomization\n  -  known platelet count < 100.000/µL at the time of screening\n  -  known anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) at the time of screening\n  -  oral anticoagulation that [NOT] cannot be safely [NOT] discontinued for the duration of the study\n  -  INR known to be greater than 1.5 at the time of screening\n  -  chronic renal insufficiency requiring dialysis\n  -  moderate [OR] or severe hepatic dysfunction (Child Pugh B [OR] or C)\n  -  increased risk of bradycardia events (Sick Sinus, [OR] AV block grade II [OR] or III, bradycardia-induced syncope)\n  -  index event is an acute complication (< 30 days) of PCI\n  -  concomitant medical illness that in the opinion of the investigator is associated with a life expectancy < 1 year\n  -  concomitant oral [OR] or i.v. therapy with strong CYP3A Inhibitors (e.g. ketoconazole, [OR] itraconazole, [OR] voriconazole, [OR] telithromycin, [OR] clarithromycin, [OR] nefazodone, [OR] ritonavir, [OR] saquinavir, [OR] nelfinavir, [OR] indinavir, [OR] atazanavir, [OR] grapefruit juice > 1 L/d), CYP3A substrates [AND] with narrow therapeutic indices (e.g. cyclosporine, [OR] quinidine), [OR] or strong CYP3A inducers (e.g. rifampin/ [OR] rifampicin, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] carbamazepine, [OR] dexamethason, [OR] phenobarbital ) that [NOT] cannot be safely [NOT] discontinued\n  -  =1 doses of ticagrelor [OR] or prasugrel within 5 days before randomisation\n  -  [NOT] no written informed consent\n  -  participation in another investigational drug study\n  -  previous enrolment in this study\n  -  for women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] no negative pregnancy test [AND] and [NOT] no agree to use reliable method of birth control during the study\n  -  Pregnancy, giving birth within the last 90 days, [OR] or lactation\n  -  [NOT] inability to cooperate with protocol requirements<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
  -  men or women aged 18 years or older
  -  subjects with Acute coronary syndrome (ACS) undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)
  -  subjects receiving ticagrelor or prasugrel during hospitalization for ACS
  -  subjects able to give written informed consent
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  intolerance of [OR] or allergy to ticagrelor [OR] or prasugrel
  -  history of any stroke, [OR] transient ischemic attack [OR] or intracranial bleeding
  -  known intracranial neoplasm, [OR] intracranial arteriovenous malformation [OR] or intracranial aneurysm
  -  active bleeding, clinical findings, that in the judgement of the investigator are associated with an increased risk of bleeding
  -  fibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 24 h before randomization, [NOT] non-fibrin-specific fibrinolytic therapy less than 48 h before randomization
  -  known platelet count < 100.000/µL at the time of screening
  -  known anemia (hemoglobin <10 g/dL) at the time of screening
  -  oral anticoagulation that [NOT] cannot be safely [NOT] discontinued for the duration of the study
  -  INR known to be greater than 1.5 at the time of screening
  -  chronic renal insufficiency requiring dialysis
  -  moderate [OR] or severe hepatic dysfunction (Child Pugh B [OR] or C)
  -  increased risk of bradycardia events (Sick Sinus, [OR] AV block grade II [OR] or III, bradycardia-induced syncope)
  -  index event is an acute complication (< 30 days) of PCI
  -  concomitant medical illness that in the opinion of the investigator is associated with a life expectancy < 1 year
  -  concomitant oral [OR] or i.v. therapy with strong CYP3A Inhibitors (e.g. ketoconazole, [OR] itraconazole, [OR] voriconazole, [OR] telithromycin, [OR] clarithromycin, [OR] nefazodone, [OR] ritonavir, [OR] saquinavir, [OR] nelfinavir, [OR] indinavir, [OR] atazanavir, [OR] grapefruit juice > 1 L/d), CYP3A substrates [AND] with narrow therapeutic indices (e.g. cyclosporine, [OR] quinidine), [OR] or strong CYP3A inducers (e.g. rifampin/ [OR] rifampicin, [OR] phenytoin, [OR] carbamazepine, [OR] dexamethason, [OR] phenobarbital ) that [NOT] cannot be safely [NOT] discontinued
  -  =1 doses of ticagrelor [OR] or prasugrel within 5 days before randomisation
  -  [NOT] no written informed consent
  -  participation in another investigational drug study
  -  previous enrolment in this study
  -  for women [AND] of childbearing potential [NOT] no negative pregnancy test [AND] and [NOT] no agree to use reliable method of birth control during the study
  -  Pregnancy, giving birth within the last 90 days, [OR] or lactation
  -  [NOT] inability to cooperate with protocol requirements
