Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nOAT required for reasons not related to AF (i.e., prosthetic valve, PV stenosis, previous pulmonary embolism, presence of spontaneous echo contrast [SEC] at standard echo performed at 3-months follow-up).\nAny cardiac surgery within the past 60 days (2 months) or valvular cardiac surgical procedure at any time (i.e., ventriculotomy, atriotomy, and valve repair or replacement and presence of a prosthetic valve)\nPrevious myocardial infarction (MI) or a percutaneous coronary intervention PCI within the past 3 months\nAwaiting cardiac transplantation or other cardiac surgery within the next 365 days (12 months)\nDocumented left atrial thrombus\nSignificant pulmonary disease, (e.g., restrictive pulmonary disease, constrictive or COPD) or any other disease or malfunction of the lungs or respiratory system that produces chronic symptoms\nSignificant medical problem that in the opinion of the investigator would preclude enrollment in this study\nWomen who are pregnant (as evidenced by pregnancy test if pre-menopausal)\nAcute illness or active systemic infection or sepsis\nUnstable angina\nContraindication to anticoagulation (i.e., heparin, warfarin or another commercially available anticoagulation medication)\nHistory of blood clotting or bleeding abnormalities\nLife expectancy less than 360 days (12 months)\nUncontrolled Heart Failure or NYHA Class III or IV heart failure\nEnrollment in a clinical study evaluating another device or drug, within the past 6 months\nUnable or unwilling to comply with protocol requirements\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nOAT required for reasons [NOT] not related to AF (i.e., prosthetic valve, [OR] PV stenosis, previous pulmonary embolism, presence of spontaneous echo contrast [SEC] at standard echo performed at 3-months follow-up).\nAny cardiac surgery within the past 60 days [OR] (2 months) or valvular cardiac surgical procedure at any time (i.e., ventriculotomy, [OR] atriotomy, [OR] and valve [OR] repair [OR] or replacement [AND] and presence of a prosthetic valve)\nPrevious myocardial infarction (MI) [OR] or a percutaneous coronary intervention PCI within the past 3 months\nAwaiting cardiac transplantation [OR] or other cardiac surgery within the next 365 days (12 months)\nDocumented left atrial thrombus\nSignificant pulmonary disease, (e.g., restrictive pulmonary disease, [OR] constrictive [OR] or COPD) [OR] or any other disease [OR] or malfunction of the lungs [OR] or respiratory system that produces chronic symptoms\nSignificant medical problem that in the opinion of the investigator would [NOT] preclude enrollment in this study\nWomen [AND] who are pregnant (as evidenced by pregnancy test if pre-menopausal)\nAcute illness [OR] or active systemic infection [OR] or sepsis\nUnstable angina\nContraindication to anticoagulation (i.e., heparin, [OR] warfarin [OR] or another commercially available anticoagulation medication)\nHistory of blood clotting [OR] or bleeding abnormalities\nLife expectancy less than 360 days (12 months)\nUncontrolled Heart Failure [OR] or NYHA Class III or IV heart failure\nEnrollment in a clinical study evaluating another device [OR] or drug, within the past 6 months\nUnable [OR] or [NOT] unwilling to comply with protocol requirements<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
OAT required for reasons [NOT] not related to AF (i.e., prosthetic valve, [OR] PV stenosis, previous pulmonary embolism, presence of spontaneous echo contrast [SEC] at standard echo performed at 3-months follow-up).
Any cardiac surgery within the past 60 days [OR] (2 months) or valvular cardiac surgical procedure at any time (i.e., ventriculotomy, [OR] atriotomy, [OR] and valve [OR] repair [OR] or replacement [AND] and presence of a prosthetic valve)
Previous myocardial infarction (MI) [OR] or a percutaneous coronary intervention PCI within the past 3 months
Awaiting cardiac transplantation [OR] or other cardiac surgery within the next 365 days (12 months)
Documented left atrial thrombus
Significant pulmonary disease, (e.g., restrictive pulmonary disease, [OR] constrictive [OR] or COPD) [OR] or any other disease [OR] or malfunction of the lungs [OR] or respiratory system that produces chronic symptoms
Significant medical problem that in the opinion of the investigator would [NOT] preclude enrollment in this study
Women [AND] who are pregnant (as evidenced by pregnancy test if pre-menopausal)
Acute illness [OR] or active systemic infection [OR] or sepsis
Unstable angina
Contraindication to anticoagulation (i.e., heparin, [OR] warfarin [OR] or another commercially available anticoagulation medication)
History of blood clotting [OR] or bleeding abnormalities
Life expectancy less than 360 days (12 months)
Uncontrolled Heart Failure [OR] or NYHA Class III or IV heart failure
Enrollment in a clinical study evaluating another device [OR] or drug, within the past 6 months
Unable [OR] or [NOT] unwilling to comply with protocol requirements
