Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nPatients with chronic heart failure of New York Heart Association Class II or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40% for patients in NYHA class II or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.\nAge =18 years\nObtained informed consent\nStable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nPatients with chronic heart failure [AND] of New York Heart Association Class II [OR] or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40%  for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.\nAge =18 years\nObtained informed consent\nStable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Patients with chronic heart failure [AND] of New York Heart Association Class II [OR] or III, a left ventricular ejection fraction of = 40%  for patients in NYHA class II [OR] or = 45% for patients in NYHA class III, a hemoglobin level at the screening visit between 9.5-13.5 g/dl, [AND] and iron deficiency, which is defined as serum ferritin level < 100µg/l [OR] or between 100 and 299 µg/l, when transferring saturation is < 20%.
Age =18 years
Obtained informed consent
Stable pharmacological therapy during the last 4 weeks (with the exception of diuretics)
