Phase 2a Inclusion 
Histological evidence: FL Grade 1-3A/ [OR] iNHL, [AND] with relapsed [OR] or refractory disease (iNHL includes LPL/ [OR] WM, [OR] MZL); aNHL, defined as DLBCL, [OR] FL Grade 3B, [OR] MCL, [OR] and transformed NHL [AND] with relapsed disease; CLL/ [OR] SLL, [OR] PTCL, [OR] or CTCL [AND] (with MF/ [OR] SS) [AND] with relapsed [OR] or refractory. 
Received BCR [OR] and/or BCL2 inhibitors were intolerant [OR] or had relapsed/ [OR] refractory disease afterwards. 
Prior treatment for lymphoid malignancy for progressive /refractory disease 
≥ 1 prior regimen (min 2 cycles) with antibody conjugate, [OR] cytotoxic chemotherapy, [OR] or TKI alone [OR] or in combination. 
Measureable disease defined as: ≥ 1 lesion ≥ 1.5 cm single dimension via CT, [OR] CT/ [OR] PET [AND] with nodal [OR] or mass lesions; Quantifiable circulating tumor cells; [OR] or for Waldenström's macroglobulinemia presence of IgM l > 2X ULN; For CTCL: mSWAT > 0 
Ability to provide diagnostic reports 
General Inclusion 
ECOG Score of 0 or 1. 
Hematologic ANC > 1000/uL [AND] and platelet > 75,000/uL, 
Serum creatinine of < 1.5 ULN [OR] or calculated CrCl of > 50 mL/min 
Bilirubin < 20.0mg/dL (if Gilberts then < 2.5 mg/dL) [AND] and AST/ [OR] AST < 2.5 ULN
