time ambulatory blood pressure measurement (ABPM) <150/95mmHg on stable doses of one or more antihypertensive medication (at least one of which should be; an ACE inhibitor, [OR] angiotensin receptor blocker [OR] or diuretic) for 3 months, [OR] or [NOT] untreated hypertensive patients with an average daytime ABPM =135/85 [AND] but <150/95.<|eot_id|>']
