Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Currently enrolled in another research trial for investigative nutritional or other therapies thought to have an impact on immune system functioning. \n2. Unable to consent to the study. \n3. Women who are pregnant or are attempting conception, especially in the presence of a history of recurrent spontaneous abortion. \n4. Other medical complications that might preclude one from participating in the study, i.e., recent heart attack or stroke or chronic kidney disease. \n5. Currently taking immunomodulatory medication, i.e. interferon. \n6. Currently taking other medications thought to have an impact on immune system functioning, i.e., chemotherapeutic agents. \n7. Known allergy to rice, rice bran, or related food products. \n8. Known allergy to mushrooms or related food products. \n9. History of malignancies related to the NK cell line, including: NK cell leukemias and T-cell large granular lymphocyte leukemias, NK-cell lymphoproliferative disease of granular lymphocytes, and NK cell lymphomas, e.g., nasal and nasal-like NK/T-cell lymphomas. \n10. Current smoker.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nExclusion Criteria:\n 1. Currently enrolled in another research trial for investigative nutritional [OR] or other therapies thought to have an impact on immune system functioning. \n 2. Unable to consent to the study. \n 3. Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or are attempting conception, especially in the presence of a history of recurrent spontaneous abortion. \n 4. Other medical complications that might [NOT] preclude one from participating in the study, i.e., recent heart attack [OR] or stroke [OR] or chronic kidney disease. \n 5. Currently taking immunomodulatory medication, i.e. interferon. \n 6. Currently taking other medications thought to have an impact on immune system functioning, i.e., chemotherapeutic agents. \n 7. Known allergy to rice, [OR] rice bran, [OR] or related food products. \n 8. Known allergy to mushrooms [OR] or related food products. \n 9. History of malignancies related to the NK cell line, including: NK cell leukemias [OR] and T-cell large granular lymphocyte leukemias, [OR] NK-cell lymphoproliferative disease [OR] of granular lymphocytes, [OR] and NK cell lymphomas, e.g., nasal [OR] and nasal-like NK/ [OR] T-cell lymphomas. \n 10. Current smoker.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Exclusion Criteria:
 1. Currently enrolled in another research trial for investigative nutritional [OR] or other therapies thought to have an impact on immune system functioning. 
 2. Unable to consent to the study. 
 3. Women [AND] who are pregnant [OR] or are attempting conception, especially in the presence of a history of recurrent spontaneous abortion. 
 4. Other medical complications that might [NOT] preclude one from participating in the study, i.e., recent heart attack [OR] or stroke [OR] or chronic kidney disease. 
 5. Currently taking immunomodulatory medication, i.e. interferon. 
 6. Currently taking other medications thought to have an impact on immune system functioning, i.e., chemotherapeutic agents. 
 7. Known allergy to rice, [OR] rice bran, [OR] or related food products. 
 8. Known allergy to mushrooms [OR] or related food products. 
 9. History of malignancies related to the NK cell line, including: NK cell leukemias [OR] and T-cell large granular lymphocyte leukemias, [OR] NK-cell lymphoproliferative disease [OR] of granular lymphocytes, [OR] and NK cell lymphomas, e.g., nasal [OR] and nasal-like NK/ [OR] T-cell lymphomas. 
 10. Current smoker.
