le NA (lamivudine, [OR] adefovir, [OR] entecavir [OR] or tenofovir) for 6 months to 5 years\nDeveloped HBeAg seroconversion (HBeAg negative [AND] and ant-HBe negative) [AND] with undetectable HBV DNA by PCR based assay on NA treatment.\nNegative urine [OR] or serum pregnancy test (for women of childbearing potential) documented within the 24-hour period prior to the first dose of test drug. Additionally, all females must be using reliable contraception during the study [AND] and for 3 months after treatment completion<|eot_id|>']
