\n\n\n### Response:\nPrimary groups: Vaccination against typhoid fever within 5 years before dosing.\nHistory of clinical typhoid fever, clinical paratyphoid A [OR] or B fever.\nImmunization with any other vaccine (oral [OR] or parenteral) within 4 weeks prior to study start [OR] or planned vaccination during the study\nCurrent intake of antibiotics [OR] or end of antibiotic therapy <8 days before first IMP administration\nChronic (longer than 14 days) administration of immunosuppressants [OR] or other immune-modifying drugs within 6 months before the first dose of investigational vaccine; oral corticosteroids in dosages of =0.5 mg/kg/d prednisolone [OR] or equivalent are [NOT] excluded; inhaled [OR] or topical steroids are allowed\nAcute [OR] or chronic clinically significant gastrointestinal disease<|eot_id|>']
Response: Primary groups: Vaccination against typhoid fever within 5 years before dosing.
History of clinical typhoid fever, clinical paratyphoid A [OR] or B fever.
Immunization with any other vaccine (oral [OR] or parenteral) within 4 weeks prior to study start [OR] or planned vaccination during the study
Current intake of antibiotics [OR] or end of antibiotic therapy <8 days before first IMP administration
Chronic (longer than 14 days) administration of immunosuppressants [OR] or other immune-modifying drugs within 6 months before the first dose of investigational vaccine; oral corticosteroids in dosages of =0.5 mg/kg/d prednisolone [OR] or equivalent are [NOT] excluded; inhaled [OR] or topical steroids are allowed
Acute [OR] or chronic clinically significant gastrointestinal disease
