Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nunstable condition, COPD exacerbation\nmild (GOLD 1) or very severe COPD (GOLD 4)\nrequirement for oxygen therapy at low altitude residence\nhypoventilation\npulmonary hypertension\nmore than mild or unstable cardiovascular disease\nuse of drugs that affect respiratory center drive\ninternal, neurologic or psychiatric disease that interfere with protocol compliance including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day), inability to perform 6 min walk test.\nprevious intolerance to moderate altitude (<2600m).\nexposure to altitudes >1500m for >2 days within the last 4 weeks before the study.\npregnant or nursing patients\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nunstable condition, [OR] COPD exacerbation\nmild (GOLD 1) [OR] or very severe COPD (GOLD 4)\nrequirement for oxygen therapy at low altitude residence\nhypoventilation\npulmonary hypertension\nmore than mild [OR] or unstable cardiovascular disease\nuse of drugs that affect respiratory center drive\ninternal, [OR] neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disease that interfere with protocol compliance including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day), [NOT] inability to perform 6 min walk test.\nprevious intolerance to moderate altitude (<2600m).\nexposure to altitudes >1500m for >2 days within the last 4 weeks before the study.\npregnant [OR] or nursing patients<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
unstable condition, [OR] COPD exacerbation
mild (GOLD 1) [OR] or very severe COPD (GOLD 4)
requirement for oxygen therapy at low altitude residence
hypoventilation
pulmonary hypertension
more than mild [OR] or unstable cardiovascular disease
use of drugs that affect respiratory center drive
internal, [OR] neurologic [OR] or psychiatric disease that interfere with protocol compliance including current heavy smoking (>20 cigarettes per day), [NOT] inability to perform 6 min walk test.
previous intolerance to moderate altitude (<2600m).
exposure to altitudes >1500m for >2 days within the last 4 weeks before the study.
pregnant [OR] or nursing patients
