File: NCT02152696_inc 

Das File: /work/eauten2s/ec_criteria_struct/chia/input/chia_text_half/NCT02152696_inc.txt wurde erfolgreich geladen.
Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nFemale with a persisting pregnancy of unknown location: \nA pregnancy of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman with a positive pregnancy test but no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. \nPersistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, or < 50% fall between the first and last value. \nPatient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL \nGreater than or 18 years of age \n\n\n### Response:\nFemale [AND] with a persisting pregnancy of unknown location: \nA pregnancy of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman [AND] with a positive pregnancy test [AND] but [NOT] no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus [OR] or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac [AND] with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus [OR] or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. \nPersistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, [OR] or < 50% fall between the first and last value. \nPatient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL \nGreater than or 18 years of age<|eot_id|>']
Response: Female [AND] with a persisting pregnancy of unknown location: 
A pregnancy of unknown location is defined as a pregnancy in a woman [AND] with a positive pregnancy test [AND] but [NOT] no definitive signs of pregnancy in the uterus [OR] or adnexa on ultrasound imaging. A definitive sign of gestation includes ultrasound visualization of a gestational sac [AND] with a yolk sac (with or without an embryo) in the uterus [OR] or in the adnexa. Ultrasound must be performed within 7 days prior to randomization. 
Persistence of hCG is defined as at least 2 serial hCG values (over 2-14 days), showing < 15% rise per day, [OR] or < 50% fall between the first and last value. 
Patient is hemodynamically stable, hemoglobin >10 mg/dL 
Greater than or 18 years of age
