Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\n1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration. \n2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, or that have a co-morbidity not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, cystic fibrosis). \n3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention or procedure or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n 1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration.\nExclusion Criteria:\n 2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may [NOT] prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, [OR] or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, [OR] or that have a co-morbidity [NOT] not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, [OR] cystic fibrosis).\n 3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention [OR] or procedure [OR] or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 1. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of CP secondary to neuronal migration.
Exclusion Criteria:
 2. Co-morbidities: Medical conditions that may [NOT] prevent the administration of rehabilitation therapies at the intensity required by the study, [OR] or that may compromise the study ability to maintain blindness, [OR] or that have a co-morbidity [NOT] not typically associated with CP (i.e. cancer, [OR] cystic fibrosis).
 3. Co-interventions: Anticipated pharmacological intervention [OR] or procedure [OR] or participation in other studies that may interfere with this study.
