Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAge <1m or > 24 months of age\nNo secure diagnosis of epilepsy\n< 4 seizures/week on average in baseline period\nTrial of < 2 AEDs\nContinues on corticosteroids in previous 3 months prior to randomisation\nMetabolic disease contraindicating use of the ketogenic diet e.g. pyruvate carboxylase deficiency, MCAD from previous medical investigation and screening at baseline.\nProgressive neurological disease\nSevere gastroesophageal reflux\nPrevious treatment with the ketogenic diet\nConcurrent participation in another clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.\nPatients who are prescribed AEDs not listed in the trial IMPs\n\n\n### Response:\nAge <1m [OR] or > 24 months of age\n[NOT] No secure diagnosis of epilepsy\n < 4 seizures/week on average in baseline period\nTrial of < 2 AEDs\nContinues on corticosteroids in previous 3 months prior to randomisation\nMetabolic disease contraindicating use of the ketogenic diet e.g. pyruvate carboxylase deficiency, [OR] MCAD from previous medical investigation [AND] and screening at baseline.\nProgressive neurological disease\nSevere gastroesophageal reflux\nPrevious treatment with the ketogenic diet\nConcurrent participation in another clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.\nPatients who are prescribed AEDs [NOT] not listed in the trial IMPs<|eot_id|>']
Response: Age <1m [OR] or > 24 months of age
[NOT] No secure diagnosis of epilepsy
 < 4 seizures/week on average in baseline period
Trial of < 2 AEDs
Continues on corticosteroids in previous 3 months prior to randomisation
Metabolic disease contraindicating use of the ketogenic diet e.g. pyruvate carboxylase deficiency, [OR] MCAD from previous medical investigation [AND] and screening at baseline.
Progressive neurological disease
Severe gastroesophageal reflux
Previous treatment with the ketogenic diet
Concurrent participation in another clinical trial of an investigational medicinal product.
Patients who are prescribed AEDs [NOT] not listed in the trial IMPs
