esponse:\nPatients who have had a prior abdominal myomectomy\nPost-menopausal women\nPatients with known bleeding/ [OR] clotting disorders\nPatients with a history of gynecologic malignancy\nHistory of allergic reactions attributed to compounds of similar chemical [OR] or biologic composition to misoprostol\nAny cases converted to abdominal hysterectomy [OR] or other additional elective surgical procedures performed at time of abdominal myomectomy will be [NOT] excluded from data analysis\nUncontrolled intercurrent illness including, but not limited to, ongoing [OR] or active infection, symptomatic congestive heart failure, unstable angina pectoris, [OR] cardiac arrhythmia, [OR] or psychiatric illness/ [OR] social situations that would limit compliance with study requirements.<|eot_id|>']
Response: Patients who have had a prior abdominal myomectomy
Post-menopausal women
Patients with known bleeding/ [OR] clotting disorders
Patients with a history of gynecologic malignancy
History of allergic reactions attributed to compounds of similar chemical [OR] or biologic composition to misoprostol
Any cases converted to abdominal hysterectomy [OR] or other additional elective surgical procedures performed at time of abdominal myomectomy will be [NOT] excluded from data analysis
Uncontrolled intercurrent illness including, but not limited to, ongoing [OR] or active infection, symptomatic congestive heart failure, unstable angina pectoris, [OR] cardiac arrhythmia, [OR] or psychiatric illness/ [OR] social situations that would limit compliance with study requirements.
