Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nAged between 18-70 years\nMeets the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM) IV and DSM-V diagnostic criteria for generalised anxiety disorder (GAD) based on structured interview (Mini International Neuropsychiatric Interview-Plus 6 [MINI-Plus 6]. Note that while the MINI-Plus 6 uses the DSM-IV criteria, the same criteria are used in the DSM-V).\nPresents with anxiety (Hamilton Anxiety Rating Scale = 18) at the time of study entry\nFluent in written and spoken English\nProvides a signed copy of the consent form\nPrimary diagnosis other than GAD\nPresentation of moderate to severe depressive symptoms (Montgomery-Asberg Rating Scale: MADRS = 18 at time of study entry or = 24 at any time during study)\nPresentation of suicidal ideation (= 3 on MADRS suicidal thoughts domain at time of study entry or at any time during study)\nCurrent diagnosis of bipolar disorder or schizophrenia on structured interview (MINI Plus)\nCurrent substance/alcohol use disorder on structured interview (MINI Plus) Page 21 of 39 Commercial-in-Confidence\nCurrently taking an antidepressant, mood stabiliser, antipsychotic, anticonvulsant, warfarin or thyroxin, or current regular use (more than 2 days per week) of a benzodiazepine or opioid-based analgesic\nCurrent use of a psychotropic nutraceutical (e.g. St John\'s wort)\nPrevious intolerance to kava\nThree or more failed trials of pharmacotherapy for the current GAD episode\nRecently commenced psychotherapy (within four weeks of study entry)\nKnown or suspected clinically unstable systemic medical disorder\nDiagnosed hepato-biliary disease/inflammation\nElevated liver enzymes at baseline blood test\nPregnancy or breastfeeding, or trying to conceive\nNot using medically approved contraception (including abstinence) if female and of childbearing age\nUnable to participate in all scheduled visits, treatment plan, or other trial procedures according to the protocol (except for the optional genetic component)\n\n\n### Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\nAged between 18-70 years\nMeets the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM) IV and DSM-V diagnostic criteria for generalised anxiety disorder (GAD) based on structured interview (Mini International Neuropsychiatric Interview-Plus 6 [MINI-Plus 6]. Note that while the MINI-Plus 6 uses the DSM-IV criteria, the same criteria are used in the DSM-V).\nPresents with anxiety (Hamilton Anxiety Rating Scale = 18) at the time of study entry\nFluent in written and spoken English\nProvides a signed copy of the consent form\nExclusion Criteria:\nPrimary diagnosis other than GAD\nPresentation of moderate to severe depressive symptoms (Montgomery-Asberg Rating Scale: MADRS = 18 at time of study entry [OR] or = 24 at any time during study)\nPresentation of suicidal ideation (= 3 on MADRS suicidal thoughts domain at time of study entry [OR] or at any time during study)\nCurrent diagnosis of bipolar disorder [OR] or schizophrenia on structured interview (MINI Plus)\nCurrent substance/ [OR] alcohol use disorder on structured interview (MINI Plus) Page 21 of 39 Commercial-in-Confidence\nCurrently taking an antidepressant, [OR] mood stabiliser, [OR] antipsychotic, [OR] anticonvulsant, [OR] warfarin [OR] or thyroxin, [OR] or current regular use (more than 2 days per week) of a benzodiazepine [OR] or opioid-based analgesic\nCurrent use of a psychotropic nutraceutical (e.g. St John\'s wort)\nPrevious intolerance to kava\nThree or more failed trials of pharmacotherapy for the current GAD episode\nRecently commenced psychotherapy (within four weeks of study entry)\nKnown [OR] or suspected clinically unstable systemic medical disorder\nDiagnosed hepato-biliary disease/ [OR] inflammation\nElevated liver enzymes at baseline blood test\nPregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or trying to conceive\n [NOT] Not using medically approved contraception (including abstinence) if female [AND] and of childbearing age\n [NOT] Unable to participate in all scheduled visits, treatment plan, [OR] or other trial procedures according to the protocol (except for the optional genetic component)<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Aged between 18-70 years
Meets the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM) IV and DSM-V diagnostic criteria for generalised anxiety disorder (GAD) based on structured interview (Mini International Neuropsychiatric Interview-Plus 6 [MINI-Plus 6]. Note that while the MINI-Plus 6 uses the DSM-IV criteria, the same criteria are used in the DSM-V).
Presents with anxiety (Hamilton Anxiety Rating Scale = 18) at the time of study entry
Fluent in written and spoken English
Provides a signed copy of the consent form
Exclusion Criteria:
Primary diagnosis other than GAD
Presentation of moderate to severe depressive symptoms (Montgomery-Asberg Rating Scale: MADRS = 18 at time of study entry [OR] or = 24 at any time during study)
Presentation of suicidal ideation (= 3 on MADRS suicidal thoughts domain at time of study entry [OR] or at any time during study)
Current diagnosis of bipolar disorder [OR] or schizophrenia on structured interview (MINI Plus)
Current substance/ [OR] alcohol use disorder on structured interview (MINI Plus) Page 21 of 39 Commercial-in-Confidence
Currently taking an antidepressant, [OR] mood stabiliser, [OR] antipsychotic, [OR] anticonvulsant, [OR] warfarin [OR] or thyroxin, [OR] or current regular use (more than 2 days per week) of a benzodiazepine [OR] or opioid-based analgesic
Current use of a psychotropic nutraceutical (e.g. St John's wort)
Previous intolerance to kava
Three or more failed trials of pharmacotherapy for the current GAD episode
Recently commenced psychotherapy (within four weeks of study entry)
Known [OR] or suspected clinically unstable systemic medical disorder
Diagnosed hepato-biliary disease/ [OR] inflammation
Elevated liver enzymes at baseline blood test
Pregnancy [OR] or breastfeeding, [OR] or trying to conceive
 [NOT] Not using medically approved contraception (including abstinence) if female [AND] and of childbearing age
 [NOT] Unable to participate in all scheduled visits, treatment plan, [OR] or other trial procedures according to the protocol (except for the optional genetic component)
