Output: ['<|begin_of_text|>Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nCreate an edited version of the following inclusion and exclusion criteria that incorporates the logical operators [AND], [OR], [NOT].\nApply these rules for inserting the logical operators:\n- Always write an [OR] before an "or", "and/or", "and / or" in the text.\n- Always write an [OR] after a comma "," and after "/" in the text.\n- Always write an [AND] before words like "with", "who", "in addition", "plus", "and", "but", "that", "despite", "having".\n- Always write a [NOT] before "no", "not", "none",  "don\'t", "free", "prevent", "Inability", "lack", "impossible", "off", "without", "unable", "naive", "excluded", "absence"\n\nGeneral rules:\n- The operators [OR], [AND], [NOT] should be written before the words like or, and, not.\n- An [AND], [OR], [NOT] must not come before a line segment (\\n).\n- Please carefully read through the given criteria text, then output only an edited version with the logical operators incorporated, enclosed in <EDITED_CRITERIA> tags.\n- Do not include any other explanations or output.\n\n\n### Input:\nSubject unwilling to cease use of any treatment for erectile dysfunction during the study, including oral medication, vacuum devices, constrictive devices, injections, urethral suppositories, gels, any over-the-counter or nonprescription medications, and products purchased via the internet\nSubject receiving dopamine agonists, nitrates, alpha-receptor blocking agents, or antihypertensive medication (see other exclusionary medications listed below)\nSubject with a history of syncope within the last 6 months prior to screening\nSubject with symptomatic postural hypotension (severe dizziness or fainting\nSubject with hypotension and a resting systolic blood pressure of < 90 mmHG or hypertension with a resting systolic blood pressure > 170 mmHG or a resting diastolic blood pressure > 110 mmHG\nSubject with any underlying cardiovascular condition, including unstable angina pectoris, which preclude sexual activity\nSubject with a history of myocardial infarction, stroke or life-threatening arrhythmia within 6 months prior to screening\nSubject with uncontrolled atrial fibrillation/flutter at screening (defined as ventricular response rate = 100 bpm)\nSubject with a bleeding disorder\nSubject with a history of prostatectomy because of prostate cancer, including nerve sparing techniques. Subjects with a history of surgical procedures for the treatment of benign prostate hypertrophy are permitted, with the exception of cryosurgery, cryotherapy or cryoablation\nSubject with hereditary degenerative retinal disorders such as retinitis pigmentosa\nSubject with a history of loss of vision because of non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy (NAION), history of temporary or permanent loss of vision, including unilateral loss of vision\nSubject with a history of congenital QT prolongation\nSubject with a penile anatomical abnormality (e.g., penile fibrosis, fractures, or Peyronie\'s disease) which, in the investigator\'s opinion, could significantly impair sexual performance. This will be based on subject\'s reported medical history (penile exam not required)\nSubject with primary hypoactive sexual desire.\nSubject with a spinal cord injury\nSubject with a severe chronic or acute liver disease, history of moderate (Child-Pugh B), or severe (Child-Pugh C) hepatic impairment\nSubject with clinically significant chronic hematological disease which could lead to priapism such as sickle cell anemia, multiple myeloma, and leukemia\nSubject with active peptic ulceration\nSubject with a history of malignancy within the past 5 years (other than squamous or basal cell skin cancer)\nSubject with a history of a positive test for Hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg) or Hepatitis C\nSubject with a known hypersensitivity to any component of the investigational medications, monoamine oxidase inhibitors, phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitors or phenylethylamines\nSubjects with a history of drug or alcohol abuse within the past 6 months\nSubjects currently consuming =5 units of alcohol per day\nSubject who is illiterate or unable to understand the Informed Consent Form, questionnaires or subject diary\nSubject who, in the opinion of the investigator, will be noncompliant with the visit schedule or study procedures\nSubject with any unstable medical, psychiatric, or substance abuse disorder that in the opinion of the investigator is likely to affect the subject\'s ability to complete the study or preclude the subject\'s participation in the study\nDiagnosis of any other neurologic disease\nUncontrolled Diabetes (Hemoglobin A1C > 7.5)\n\n\n### Response:\nSubject unwilling to cease use of any treatment for erectile dysfunction during the study, including oral medication, [OR] vacuum devices, [OR] constrictive devices, [OR] injections, [OR] urethral suppositories, [OR] gels, any over-the-counter [OR] or nonprescription medications, [OR] and products purchased via the internet\nSubject receiving dopamine agonists, [OR] nitrates, [OR] alpha-receptor blocking agents, [OR] or antihypertensive medication (see other exclusionary medications listed below)\nSubject with a history of syncope within the last 6 months prior to screening\nSubject with symptomatic postural hypotension (severe dizziness [OR] or fainting\nSubject with hypotension [OR] and a resting systolic blood pressure of < 90 mmHG [OR] or hypertension [AND] with a resting systolic blood pressure > 170 mmHG [OR] or a resting diastolic blood pressure > 110 mmHG\nSubject with any underlying cardiovascular condition, including unstable angina pectoris, which [NOT] preclude sexual activity\nSubject with a history of myocardial infarction, [OR] stroke [OR] or life-threatening arrhythmia within 6 months prior to screening\nSubject with uncontrolled atrial fibrillation/ [OR] flutter at screening (defined as ventricular response rate = 100 bpm)\n Subject with a bleeding disorder\n Subject with a history of prostatectomy because of prostate cancer, including nerve sparing techniques. Subjects with a history of surgical procedures for the treatment of benign prostate hypertrophy are permitted, with the exception of cryosurgery, [OR] cryotherapy [OR] or cryoablation\n Subject with hereditary degenerative retinal disorders such as retinitis pigmentosa\n Subject with a history of loss of vision because of [NOT] non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy (NAION), history of temporary [OR] or permanent loss of vision, including unilateral loss of vision\n Subject with a history of congenital QT prolongation\n Subject with a penile anatomical abnormality (e.g., penile fibrosis, [OR] fractures, [OR] or Peyronie\'s disease) which, in the investigator\'s opinion, could significantly impair sexual performance. This will be based on subject\'s reported medical history (penile exam not required)\n Subject with primary hypoactive sexual desire.\n Subject with a spinal cord injury\n Subject with a severe chronic [OR] or acute liver disease, history of moderate (Child-Pugh B), [OR] or severe (Child-Pugh C) hepatic impairment\n Subject with clinically significant chronic hematological disease which could lead to priapism such as sickle cell anemia, [OR] multiple myeloma, [OR] and leukemia\n Subject with active peptic ulceration\n Subject with a history of malignancy within the past 5 years (other than squamous [OR] or basal cell skin cancer)\n Subject with a history of a positive test for Hepatitis B surface antigen (HbsAg) [OR] or Hepatitis C\n Subject with a known hypersensitivity to any component of the investigational medications, [OR] monoamine oxidase inhibitors, [OR] phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitors [OR] or phenylethylamines\n Subjects with a history of drug [OR] or alcohol abuse within the past 6 months\n Subjects currently consuming =5 units of alcohol per day\n Subject who is illiterate [OR] or unable to understand the Informed Consent Form, questionnaires or subject diary\n Subject who, in the opinion of the investigator, will be [NOT] noncompliant with the visit schedule [OR] or study procedures\n Subject with any unstable medical, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] or substance abuse disorder that, in the opinion of the investigator, is likely to affect the subject\'s ability to complete the study [OR] or [NOT] preclude the subject\'s participation in the study\nDiagnosis of any other neurologic disease\n Uncontrolled Diabetes (Hemoglobin A1C > 7.5)<|eot_id|>']
