l by both the investigator and to the sponsor. No change in dose or regimen will be permitted during the study that is, from the Screening visit until the follow-up visit \nParticipant has a history of spontaneous, prolonged or severe bleeding of unclear origin \nParticipant has a history of epilepsy or fits or unexplained black-outs other than vasovagal collapse       \n    \n\n\n### Response:\nParticipant has a clinically significant abnormal physical examination, [OR] vital signs [OR] or 12 lead ECG (including QTc greater than (>) 450msec, Left Bundle Branch Block, permanent pacemaker [OR] or implantable cardioverter defibrillator) at Screening [OR] or admission \nParticipant has a history [OR] of or current liver [OR] or renal insufficiency; significant cardiac, [OR] vascular, [OR] pulmonary, [OR] gastrointestinal, [OR] endocrine, [OR] neurologic, [OR] hematologic, [OR] rheumatologic, [OR] psychiatric, [OR] or metabolic disturbances \nUse of any prescription [OR] or over-the-counter medication, [OR] herbal medication, [OR] vitamins, [OR] or mineral supplements within 14 days prior to study drug administration (not including paracetamol). Medication for chronic use in age related disease will be allowed after approval by both the investigator and to the sponsor. [NOT] No change in dose [OR] or regimen will be permitted during the study that is, from the Screening visit until the follow-up visit \nParticipant has a history of spontaneous, [OR] prolonged [OR] or severe bleeding [OR] of unclear origin \nParticipant has a history of epilepsy [OR] or fits [OR] or unexplained black-outs other than vasovagal collapse<|eot_id|>']
